From bd437fd2656236c33b55e40ce745700514b317db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Radiarch Project <radiarch@invalid>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:27:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] GPU transport prototype: nuclear interactions and
 secondaries

The GPU path now follows Compute_Nuclear_interaction: proton-proton and ICRU elastic scattering, inelastic events
with secondary protons, deuterons and alphas (on a per-thread stack, transported before the next primary; a full
stack is counted), recoils deposited locally, mixtures by component. Particles carry their mass and charge through
the electromagnetic physics as hadron_step does. The secondaries' emission angles are sampled at the secondary's
table energy, as the CPU path does with radiarch's patch for upstream issue #42; the angle index is clamped into
ICRU_angles and a clamp is counted (none expected).
---
 src/gpu_api.h        |  27 +-
 src/gpu_glue.c       |  95 ++++++-
 src/gpu_transport.cu | 605 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------------
 3 files changed, 549 insertions(+), 178 deletions(-)

